riffs even suspend the whole  trade agreement  and also you say you won't renegotiate  the text of the treaty but if that could  open some further doors to compromise  why won't you do that  i think i will start with the with the  second part of your questions i'm sure  that you've been  uh following the the the brexit  negotiations in a great detail and you  know that it took us  more than four four years to find that  delicate compromise where first and  foremost  we took the interest of the northern  ireland people  into  most appropriate account because for us  what was the of paramount importance was  to protect the peace and stability in  the in the northern ireland to avoid the  hard border  on the island and protect the the single  market and we've been pondering over  these issues for years this was the best  solution which we found together i have  to say that  concrete  northern ireland unique  solution we've been developing at the  expresswish of the uk government  we after laborious negotiations where  we've been really going  through the very demanding text line by  line  we agreed upon that  we  sign it it was ratified and  now we cannot we cannot imagine that we  can come up with something better which  would correspond to this three  priorities peace no hard border  protection of the eu single market on  top of it  giving the northern ireland people and  operators this unique opportunity to to  have access to 500 million potential  customers which is the only place in the  world which has it  and  therefore we are ready to  show that uh the agreements we  negotiated the protocol we agreed upon  offers us enough  uh legal and political space to make  sure that the operations could be smooth  that the checks could be inobtrusive if  we finally get the proper access to the  to the it and to the to the to the data  we are talking indeed about very very  limited uh  checks with a three-page certificate  with uh  i would say a few  a few few tracks being 