ete terms  concerning the trustee trader scheme so  there is a lot of opportunities what we  could do and how we could tackle this  issue so we expect that also the debate  uh in the british parliament be it in  the house of commons and house of lords  will take some time of course  if this draft bill  will become the law then of course i  cannot exclude anything  but we are not there yet and we want to  solve this issue  as the two partners should  through negotiations  looking for the common ground and  delivering for the people in northern  ireland  okay i'll take one final question joe  thank you joe barnes from the daily  telegraph um so one of london's main  complaints with the current protocol is  that while it's an operation the dup  will not enter storm on and that's why  they're saying it doesn't respect the  good friday agreement  um so do you think the uk government is  being disingenuous with that or will you  be willing to potentially move further  by putting stuff uh extra stuff into law  maybe adding changing the eu's customs  laws to accommodate  more changes on northern line or do  something to proclaim the dep or do you  have another plan for kind of convincing  the dup to come into stormont  to kind of please the british government  thank you  of course forming the the the  uh the assembly and the executive  it's uh for the people of northern  ireland to decide it's uh for the  uk uh  government  uh to work on with the political parties  in northern ireland we have no intention  to interfere in this process we've been  very clear from the beginning and uh i  think the protocol it's absolutely  explicit on that that we respect first  and foremost good friday belfast  agreement in all its dimension and we  respect also uh constitutional and  territorial arrangements of the uk so i  we cannot be clear on on that fact and  as you know i i have uh the regular  meetings with the political leaders in  northern ireland and i was very explicit  and i will